[2026-06-19T15:09:40.233805] [CREATED] [T073] {"title": "When you re-open a task from \"Review\" this looks unreadable in dark mode <div class=\"form-group\" style=\"background: #e8f5e9; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px;\"><label style=\"color: #27ae60;\">Previous Fix</label><p>Fixed motherboards.html: The showImageModal function was defined inside an IIFE (Immediately Invoked Function Expression) which made it inaccessible to global scope. Added 'window.showImageModal = showImageModal' at the end of the function to expose it to the global scope so onclick handlers can access it. This fixes the 'showImageModal is not defined' error when clicking on listing images.</p></div>", "column": "problems", "category": "", "priority": "Medium"}
